    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a pretty strong stance you're taking there. you're saying the critics are just wrong or resistant to change? i've seen some pretty intense debate lately about whether the data actually supports those claims or if the studies are just biased. what do the actual counter-arguments look like? like, what are the specific reasons people say it doesn't work?",
